option.QUALITY=Quality
option.QUALITY.comment=Sample counts of shadows, ambient occlusion, reflections and the sky.
option.SHADOWS=Shadows
option.SHADOWS.comment=Shadows from the sun and moon.
option.COLORED_SHADOWS=Coloured Shadows
option.COLORED_SHADOWS.comment=Light through stained glass and water takes on its colour.
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Sharper shadows at a higher cost.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far shadows are drawn, in blocks.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Width of the soft shadow edge (Soft style only).
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Path Angle
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Tilt of the sun path; a tilt gives longer, more interesting shadows.
option.SSAO=Ambient Occlusion
option.SSAO.comment=Soft darkening in corners and crevices.
option.SSAO_STRENGTH=Ambient Occlusion Strength
option.SURFACE_SHEEN=Sun Sheen
option.SURFACE_SHEEN.comment=Blocks reflect the sun by their material: metals and polished stone shine, stone and wood a little, dirt and sand not at all.
option.GENERATED_NORMALS=Texture Relief
option.GENERATED_NORMALS.comment=Blocks take the light by the relief of their own texture, pixel by pixel, instead of as flat painted faces.
option.GENERATED_NORMAL_STRENGTH=Texture Relief Depth
option.GLOSSY_REFLECTIONS=Glossy Reflections
option.GLOSSY_REFLECTIONS.comment=Metals, polished stone, glazed blocks and gems mirror the sky and the world around them.
option.HANDHELD_LIGHT=Handheld Light
option.HANDHELD_LIGHT.comment=A torch in hand lights up the surroundings.
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_WARMTH=Torch Light Warmth
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_WARMTH.comment=0 = neutral white, higher = warmer, more orange.
option.AMBIENT_MIN=Darkness Floor
option.AMBIENT_MIN.comment=Minimum light in caves and at night.
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Grass, flowers and crops sway in the wind.
option.WAVING_LEAVES=Waving Leaves
option.WAVING_LEAVES.comment=Leaves and vines rustle in the wind.
option.WIND_STRENGTH=Wind Strength
option.WIND_STRENGTH.comment=Stronger in rain and storms.
option.FOLIAGE_TRANSLUCENCY=Foliage Translucency
option.FOLIAGE_TRANSLUCENCY.comment=Sunlight shines through leaves and grass.
option.WET_SURFACES=Wet Surfaces
option.WET_SURFACES.comment=Rain darkens the ground and gives it a soft sheen.
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Off, sky only, or sky and the world around.
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Water Refraction
option.WATER_REFRACTION.comment=The bottom wobbles under the waves.
option.WATER_WAVE_STRENGTH=Wave Strength
option.WATER_CLARITY=Water Clarity
option.WATER_CLARITY.comment=How far you can see into the water.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Caustics
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment=Moving veins of sunlight on the bottom of shallow water.
option.WATER_FOAM=Shore Foam
option.WATER_FOAM.comment=Broken foam on water that is barely a block deep.
option.CLOUDS=Clouds
option.CLOUDS.comment=Off, flat like vanilla Fast clouds, or blocky 3D clouds you can fly through. Their shapes come from the game's cloud texture.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_SIZE=Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT=Cloud Height
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=Stretches the cloud cubes upwards (1 = vanilla proportions).
option.CLOUD_SIZE.comment=Size of the cloud cubes compared to vanilla (1 = vanilla 12 x 12 x 4 blocks); same shapes, more volume.
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS=Light Shafts
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment=Rays of light through gaps when looking towards the sun.
option.LIGHT_SHAFT_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Distance haze, rain fog and morning mist.
option.VALLEY_MIST=Morning Mist
option.VALLEY_MIST.comment=Low mist in valleys at sunrise and in rain.
option.LOW_HAZE=Ground Mist
option.LOW_HAZE.comment=Banks of low cloud lying on water, swamps and low land in the distance, thickest in the morning and evening.
option.FAR_HAZE=Distant Haze
option.FAR_HAZE.comment=A light veil of air over far-away land beyond the loaded chunks.
option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment=Soft glow around bright lights.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom Strength
option.LENS_FLARE=Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment=Faint coloured reflections of the sun in the camera lens when looking towards it.
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=Lens Flare Strength
option.EXPOSURE=Brightness
option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.WARMTH=Warmth
option.WARMTH.comment=Warm, cosy colour tint.
option.FXAA=Anti-Aliasing
option.FXAA.comment=Smooths jagged edges (FXAA).
screen.LIGHTING=Lighting
screen.NATURE=Nature
screen.WATER=Water
screen.SKY=Sky and Fog
screen.POST=Image
screen.WEATHER=Weather
option.MOD_WEATHER=Weather from Pocky Mods
option.MOD_WEATHER.comment=With Petrichor, Hoarfrost and Rustling Leaves installed the shaders show their weather: rain from drizzle to downpour, sun showers under a blue sky, ground that stays wet and dries after the rain, their lightning, snow kinds and blizzards, plants bending in their wind. Off: vanilla weather only.
option.WEATHER_GRADING=Weather Colours
option.WEATHER_GRADING.comment=Every weather has its own light: golden sun showers, fresher colours after the rain, crisp snowy land, a colourless white-out in a blizzard.
option.RAINBOWS=Rainbows
option.RAINBOWS.comment=A rainbow opposite the sun in sun showers and when some rains clear up in daylight (Petrichor decides when; without it now and then after a daytime rain).
option.SNOW_SPARKLE=Snow Sparkle
option.SNOW_SPARKLE.comment=Snow glitters in the sun and moonlight: single pixels catch the light and twinkle as you move.
screen.DEBUG=Debug
option.DEBUG_VIEW=Debug View
option.DEBUG_VIEW.comment=Render sources: red = vanilla chunks, blue = Distant Horizons, green = water. Magenta or white = both drew the same pixel.
value.DEBUG_VIEW.0=Off
value.DEBUG_VIEW.1=Render Sources
profile.LOW=Low
profile.MEDIUM=Medium
profile.HIGH=High
profile.ULTRA=Ultra
value.QUALITY.0=Low
value.QUALITY.1=Medium
value.QUALITY.2=High
value.QUALITY.3=Ultra
value.WATER_REFLECTIONS.0=Off
value.WATER_REFLECTIONS.1=Sky
value.WATER_REFLECTIONS.2=Sky and World
value.CLOUDS.0=Off
value.CLOUDS.1=Flat
value.CLOUDS.2=Blocky
option.SHADOW_STYLE=Shadow Style
value.SHADOW_STYLE.0=Soft
value.SHADOW_STYLE.1=Pixel
option.SHADOW_STYLE.comment=Pixel: crisp shadows on the texel grid of the textures, like the game itself (faster). Soft: filtered shadows with soft edges.
option.SHADOW_LIGHT=Shadow Brightness
option.SHADOW_LIGHT.comment=How much sunlight still reaches shaded places. 0 = realistic dark shade.
option.LIGHT_RESPONSE=Vanilla Light
option.LIGHT_RESPONSE.comment=How close bright sunlight stays to the game's own colours. 0 = physical light (much brighter noon).
option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT=Volumetric Light
option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT.comment=Sunbeams through leaves, clouds and fog in hazy air, and columns of light under water.
option.VOLUMETRIC_STRENGTH=Volumetric Light Strength
option.CAVE_FOG=Cave Fog
option.CAVE_FOG.comment=The far parts of caves sink into a deep dark; the air around torches and lava glows.
option.CAVE_FOG_DENSITY=Cave Fog Density
option.UNDERWATER_WOBBLE=Underwater Sway
option.UNDERWATER_WOBBLE.comment=Under water the view sways gently with the water.
